{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1478680-dragon-s-nest","id":1478680,"title":"Dragon's nest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-12T06:35:49-07:00","id":1478680,"title":"Dragon's nest","content":"How a Dragon's Nest should look like? What can happen and why should be dangerous to get into (book says that Ordo's neonates are sent into a nest to try them)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T07:08:40-07:00","id":1478684,"title":"","content":"IIRC correctly, a Dragon's Nest can be pretty much any spooky or occult location. So if the Ordo stumbles upon a Locus or Hallow, it could be that, but it could also be a haunted house or a garden infested by blood-sucking plants. So it could look like anything. The real question is, what role do you want it to play in your story or for your character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T07:27:23-07:00","id":1478686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1478680-dragon-s-nest?p=1478684#post1478684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC correctly, a Dragon's Nest can be pretty much any spooky or occult location. So if the Ordo stumbles upon a Locus or Hallow, it could be that, but it could also be a haunted house or a garden infested by blood-sucking plants. So it could look like anything. The real question is, what role do you want it to play in your story or for your character?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far I'm having it interferring with the Blood Sorecery of an elder who has his church/domain built upon a newly created nest (e.g.: viate reliquaries unexpecting expelling blood during masses etc.). This is attracting attentions of many NPCs (for different reasons) and PCs got deeply involved in this plot (which at the beginning was supposed to be only boundary.<br /> Now I'd like to get some good tips/inspirations as it will be probably deepen by characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T10:24:45-07:00","id":1478701,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would do blood seeping into the cracks and seams of the church's stonework. Any vitae lost or spilt within the church is just gone and Blood Sorcery doesn't work at all because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T11:10:42-07:00","id":1478704,"title":"","content":"Metatextually many Dragon's Nests are heavily implied to be Loci, Verges, and other supernatural stomping grounds seen through the limited understanding of the vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T09:56:44-07:00","id":1479016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1478680-dragon-s-nest?p=1478686#post1478686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far I'm having it interferring with the Blood Sorecery of an elder who has his church/domain built upon a newly created nest (e.g.: viate reliquaries unexpecting expelling blood during masses etc.). This is attracting attentions of many NPCs (for different reasons) and PCs got deeply involved in this plot (which at the beginning was supposed to be only boundary.<br /> Now I'd like to get some good tips/inspirations as it will be probably deepen by characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can look for inspiration almost anywhere. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> said a Nest is actually a placeholder name the Ordo uses for any place with mystical properties. Loci are Dragon Nests, but gates to the Underworld are, too, as are Supernal ruins, goblin markets, God Machine infrastructure, and even the strange places in that old 1st edition supplement. If you look for urban legends, creepy pastas or SCPs about weird places where strange things happen, they're all valid as Dragon Nests. It may be that some members of the Ordo do understand the fine distinctions between several classes of supernatural places, or they may be completely on the dark about it, what is relevant here is that they call all such places Dragon Nests for ease of definition and setup shop to study them and their effects in the Ordo's experiments.<br /> <br /> One simple approach you can take is to write down a reference list of things that may happen there without going into details, and then just let the PCs do the job of expanding it. Have then ask questions and test hypothesis, and develop things further as you figure out the results of their tests. <b>Do not</b> answer their questions, but note them down to help you figure up interesting answers. They don't need to ever know what exactly a given Dragon Nest is (or even that they're not all the same thing) as long as the investigation and mystery gives you a sufficient story, so you don't need to worry about reaching a definite conclusion either, just don't make the place so random as to <i>feel</i> like you're just making shit up and never bothering with consistency in the first place.<br /> <br /> Another option would be to just get one such place from another game or media and port it to your game as is. Dragon Nests are good to have things that follow rules that aren't native to Requiem, much less intuitive to vampires. Take another game-line and borrow any special place you want from them, then follow through: the place behaves exactly as it should according to that line's rules and attract the exact same type of phenomena and entities. Likewise you can do with any weird place from other works of fiction you find interesting.<br /> <br /> Remember that at the end of the day the world of CoD is one of weirdness and mystery. While a splat gives us a lot of supernatural stuff to work with that follow consistent rules related to that splat, this is still a world where things that <b>really</b> have no explanation just happen from time to time. There are things no splat knows shit about, there are things that truly are unique. So don't worry too much about following the rules of something that already exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T23:21:35-07:00","id":1480807,"title":"","content":"Hi! I am a writer and I remember I had written some <a href=\"https://papermasters.org/definition-essay\" target=\"_blank\">definition essay</a><span style=\"color:#0E101A\"> papers </span>on this theme. I posted them to my blog so if you want you can visit it to read them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27413-giiiiina","name":"giiiiina","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}